# Boundary-reference validation before selected generation

This single-file Source proposal restores the existing concrete missing-target
validation contract. It calls the unchanged resolve_surface_boundary_target
once per declared surface, in original declared order, before public generation.
The actual returned IDs are moved alongside the same surface into initialization.

An invalid Surface/Zone reference returns its existing specific RuntimeError.
A valid interzone reference still reaches selected binding and remains genuinely
UnsupportedBoundary. This does not broaden CON-01, supply coefficients, activate
legacy fallback or change any boundary temperature/flux operation.

The existing missing-interzone-target runtime regression remains the relevant
failure contract. The separate test-phase hold adds a true ordinary unsupported
regression and an explicitly authored diagnostic boundary test. No new framework
or synthetic owner is introduced here.

Before bytes are the current actual Source. Root must FULL review this production
validation-order change and obtain an independent peer before any application.
No canonical edits, project imports, formatter, Cargo, test, engine, payload,
binary, weather or Git actions were performed. No numerical or gate PASS claimed.
